{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/790382-spirit-of-magic","id":790382,"title":"Spirit of magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-21T11:46:13-08:00","id":790382,"title":"Spirit of magic","content":"Hi<br /> I had been pretty good with spirits in 1st edition (spriits resembling animals, emotions and also some conceptuals were easy for me to imagine and also see for fitting stats,...).<br /> But currently in the 2nd edition I have engaged in a discussion with a player who would like a spirit of magic to be a familiar.<br /> As they follow the normal rules of familiars I'm going to use the spirit rules to the fullest to represent it.<br /> <br /> Only thing that is in question is: How can I imagine a spirit of magic?<br /> (In the past I did death spirits, snake spirits, hate, fear, darkness,.... with ease but for a magic spirit I'm drawing blank atm)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:57:23-08:00","id":790386,"title":"","content":"A pixie or fairy, wisps of light, a talking book or just an eldritch-looking tome. A wand, a magicians hat or full on black suit, cape, top-hat and wand clothing an invisible person. A cauldron, an athame, various runes,glyphs, symbols, amulets, objects related to the magic involved, almost anything from a blue Magic the Gathering card. You might have the player narrow down the focus, where'd this magic spirit come from, what kind of magic created it, to help you figure out things from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:03:30-08:00","id":790393,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't create a spirit of 'magic' - I'd want something much more specific than that, and associated with the physical things used in the magic or the off-casts of it. Fear off someone using supernatural powers to spread terror, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:15:46-08:00","id":790404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/790382-spirit-of-magic#post790382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only thing that is in question is: How can I imagine a spirit of magic?<br /> (In the past I did death spirits, snake spirits, hate, fear, darkness,.... with ease but for a magic spirit I'm drawing blank atm)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What type of magic? Magic comes in many different traditions, each steeped in its own symbolism. A good way to answer what type of magic is asking where he found the spirit. Artificial choir spirits could easily include awakened spirits of grimoires, tarot deck, or any other number of mystical tools. Nature/elemental/location choir spirits might include an ancient oak danced around in rites, a spirit of a pond where people were drown in druidic sacrifices, or an animal spirit of an owl, raven, or other tradition appropriate creature that has be ceremonially invoked until they've eaten enough resonance tainted with 'magic' or 'ceremonial' resonance that they've become that type of spirit. The same is true of conceptual spirits, though these I envision being conceptual because they are tied to an event or action, like a research information spirit which is centered on magical subjects, or perhaps the emotion spirit tied to a particular type of magic like Foul-Cursing-Hate spirit, or Rapturous-Religious-Faith Spirit.<br /> <br /> The key to understanding spirits is to understand they can only eat what they are, or what is symbolically appropriate for them to eat (such as wolf spirits eating deer spirits, store spirits eating money spirits, depression spirits devouring joy spirits, ect...) to remain themselves. If they eat anything else it skews them. This makes the practice of feeding spirits often an act of slowing transforming the spirit. Many mages and various thaumaturges feed spirits to get favors when they can get away with it (Sometimes feeding bears results in a mauling by said bear and the same is true of spirits, or being rebuked by the warden -read: Uratha). This plausibly makes feed back loops of the spirits that exploit this essence source developing bans that make them more easy to manipulate with sacrificial essence offerings, thus making them more tempting targets to feed in this fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-21-2015, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:20:50-08:00","id":790410,"title":"","content":"Ok that was then probably the problem I had with the imaging thus magic by itself is too broad there. <br /> <br /> tnx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link"